# Architecture: which rules apply to which path

`AGENTS.md` holds rules that every file obeys. This page narrows them per path
so an agent editing one file does not have to read every document.

The table is the source of truth for **where** a rule applies. For **what** the
rule is, follow the linked document; when the two disagree, the document wins
and this table is fixed in the same change.

## Which rules apply to this path

| Path | Read before editing | Extra rules that apply only here |
|---|---|---|
| `{{ frontend_source_root }}/app/` | [frontend.md](frontend.md) | Composition root only; route adapters contain imports and re-exports, no markup or copy |
| `{{ frontend_source_root }}/pages/*/model/content.ts` | [frontend.md](frontend.md) | Page copy lives here, not in JSX |
| `{{ frontend_source_root }}/shared/ui/` | [frontend.md](frontend.md), [security.md](security.md) | Business-agnostic only; no data fetching; accessible primitives land here |
| `{{ frontend_source_root }}/shared/api/` | [frontend.md](frontend.md) | Generated types only; typed client and error mapping live here |
| `{{ frontend_root }}/eslint.config.mjs`, `docs/architecture/frontend.verify.mjs` | [frontend.md](frontend.md) | The two FSD rule sets must agree; changing a boundary rule requires an ADR |
| `docs/product/business-rules.md` | — | A rule change needs the rule owner's approval; IDs are stable |
| `docs/architecture/decisions/` | `decisions/000-template.md` | Decided ADRs are never edited; supersede with a new one |
| `AGENTS.md`, this file | — | A rule change here is an architecture change: say why in the PR, and keep every command verifiable |

## Adding a path

Add a row when a path has a rule that does not apply repository-wide, or when
it is edited often enough that "read everything first" is too expensive. Every
row must link to a document that exists; a row pointing at a missing file is a
bug.

An agent whose path is **not** in this table follows `AGENTS.md` only and says
so rather than inventing a rule.
